S643 Goldbach/Lemoine Same-Pair Bridge
======================================

Linear carrier
--------------
Even shadow: E = p + q, unordered for odd-prime pairs.
Odd shadow:  O = a + 2*b, ordered because b is doubled.
Same-pair reconstruction from (E,O): doubled prime b=O-E; single prime a=2E-O.
Validity window: E < O < 2E, with a,b odd primes.
For an unordered pair {p,q}, the odd companions are O=E+p and O=E+q.
Duplicate branch p=q: E=2p, O=3p; the two odd orientations fold together.
Boundary: q=2 Lemoine reps are apex reps and do not share an even Goldbach pair.

First duplicate/branch pairs
----------------------------
p -> (even=2p, odd=3p): 3->(6,9), 5->(10,15), 7->(14,21), 11->(22,33), 13->(26,39), 17->(34,51), 19->(38,57), 23->(46,69), 29->(58,87), 31->(62,93), 37->(74,111), 41->(82,123), 43->(86,129), 47->(94,141), 53->(106,159)
The prime 2 is exceptional: 2->(4,6), but 6 is even, so it exits the odd bridge.

