New applications
----------------
1. Treat (E,O) as a linear Vieta carrier: same-pair Goldbach/Lemoine data reconstructs the ordered prime pair exactly.
2. Use the duplicate line (2p,3p) as the ramification/branch locus, analogous to discriminant zero in the pi/e carrier.
3. Track q=2 Lemoine reps as apex boundary terms; they are odd representations without an even same-pair companion.
4. Build an even-odd companion graph and jackknife duplicate, twin-gap, and q=2 boundary channels separately.
